what's up guys the Apple event just  ended so we're gonna chat about the new  MacBook Pros that they launched and a  few other things that they talked about  in the event we look pretty short  defense I felt like I mean I think we  all knew that this was basically just an  event focusing on the MacBook Pros I  thought there might be some other things  I always hope that there's going to be  one more thing but I think the one more  thing is is no more still cross my  fingers every event and just hope and  just help so here's the new MacBook Pro  it comes in two sizes two colors 15 inch  and a 13 inch and the silver that we're  all used to and the Space Gray which the  color itself isn't new but for the  MacBook Pros it is new one of the  biggest differences here is the touch  bar so what's cool about the touch bar  is it will change with each application  that you open on your computer so here's  some of the different use cases so for  photos you can scroll through and you  can also edit and rotate and do all  kinds of different things that normally  I mean you would just do them it's not a  percent not necessary but it's a hundred  percent cool here's some uses for final  cut scrubbing the timeline that's going  to be really cool for me like I'm pretty  excited about that I do wish that this  bar was moved closer to the trackpad  basically kind of like the little tiny  bar that pops up here for mail whatever  you're on your iPhone and you're typing  it kind of gives you a little  autocorrect and things that it thinks  that you're going to say sorry this is  what I really liked in Safari you can go  through and you can switch tabs so you  can just click and it gives you a little  preview of each one key notes I don't  really ever make keynote presentations  but if I did this would all be very very  helpful you can also customize it to  anything that you might want it to be so  if there's things that you use more  often than others you can just drag and  drop those in so that's pretty cool 130  percent faster and percent faster flash  storage ten hours of battery life of  course I think the last one they said it  was also ten hours of battery life but  if you're doing high processor-intensive  things like video editing or any types  of stuff like that it definitely does  lower your battery life so I feel like  you'll probably get maybe half of that  maybe some new speakers here's the  problem for me  and for a lot of people the most  versatile port ever Thunderbolt 3 so  there's four different ports thankfully  they left us a headphone jack thank you  unfortunately they did remove the SD  card reader and for a lot of people who  do video production who are  photographers most of those people we  all use these SD card slots quite a lot  and it is so convenient to have that  port just readily accessible throw that  card in and you're ready to go well  that's removed and they only have these  four Thunderbolt three ports which  thankfully they are compatible with USB  see they also remove the MagSafe charger  and for me the MagSafe has saved my  computer's lives so many times and I'm a  little bit nervous to see how that goes  the USB Secord that it charges with is  really stiff so it's not kind of that  loose cord that you're used to having  with your other chargers I'm hoping that  they do make MagSafe USB C charger that  would be incredible the upside that  though is you can charge from any of the  ports so any of those slots you're able  to charge from which is great but let's  MagSafe in love you can simultaneously  connect to 5k displays to raid systems  Thunderbolt my guys so you basically can  just create like this crazy workstation  off of this little guy  so the 13-inch starts at $14.99 all the  way up to 1999 and the 15-inch $23.99 to  $27.99 you can get these in the Space  Gray or the silver I ended up getting  the 15-inch Space Gray so I'm excited to  see what that looks like I've never had  the Space Gray before so it's a nice  little change all in all I think the  MacBook is going to be a huge upgrade  especially for me for editing I'm a  little bit concerned about the lack of  ports because I do use those so often  for so many different things so I ended  up having to get all of the adapters for  my hard drive for now an SD card reader  fact that it is a lot smaller is going  to be pretty awesome and I'm hoping that  that kind of makes up for the fact that  they removed all of the ports and now  I'm gonna have to carry a lot of extra  things with me but I think that  eventually we'll all get over it it's  just going to take some time here you  are some different examples of using the  touch bar you can accept face times  right from the touch bar another thing  that was pretty cool is you can use  touch ID so they mentioned this in the  apple event where you can use touch ID  eels with multiple people they didn't  say how many people you could do it up  to but if you have guest accounts on  your MacBook Pro you can just have  someone come up touch it and it'll  switch to their account that's a pretty  cool feature nobody else uses my macbook  so I don't really have to use that but  you can also use Apple pay and there she  is  the new MacBook Pro your side-by-side  the 15 inch and the 13 inch the 13 is  nice I like it a lot but for editing and  other things I definitely more screen  space so a couple of other cool  highlights that happened during the  event Tim was talking about the new  Apple TV app that they're calling TV  which is I don't know you just basically  called it what it is so I mean that  works for me they talked about Minecraft  on Apple TV they also showed this really  cool demo of Apple TV which will as you  can see here Twitter showing a demo with  Apple TV app which can show an NFL game  alongside of live tweets news and more  that's kind of cool because it really is  a whole new way to watch TV most of us  who watch TV myself included at least  this is how I watch TV I'm on Twitter  the entire time reading what other  people are talking about so it was cool  about this as they were showing live  tweets of people at the game live  periscopes of people reacting to this so  it's adding this full other element of  live TV right onto your TV my favorite  quote ever we want Apple TV to be the  one place to access all of your  television today we're announcing a new  app and we simply call it TV so they did  a demo of the new Apple TV stuff and  they were talking about this week  marking the 25th anniversary of their  first notebook October 25th seventy  percent thinner 2x larger trackpad and  basically the rest of the event was just  talking about the mac books it just felt  like there should have been something  else I really thought they were going to  announce another thing they did talk  about one of the LG displays here  is a department LG to make a 5k monitor  powered by USB C so that's that right  there but that's it so I think that  probably crushes all of the hopes and  dreams that we all may have had that  Apple was going to release another  display I feel like at this point it  doesn't really make sense for them when  they just had somebody else create this  one for them so that's a new MacBook Pro  I'd love to know what you guys think of  it I think it's pretty cool I'm still  waiting patiently for the air pods to be  released it was supposed to be that late  October it's October 27th don't think  that's happening clearly anytime soon  we'll see you guys in the next video  have a great day peace we've got a new  gate in town guys I am excited to bring  you crack gate that's what I'm calling  it so the other day my friend Ed was  like hey does your phone do this and he  held it up to my ear and just slightly  went like this

